---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Resize from '@/components/motion/scenes/Resize.astro';
import ResizeControls from '@/components/motion/scenes/ResizeControls.astro';
import { MotionLayoutReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-layout.tsx';
import { MotionLayoutAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-layout.ts';
import MotionLayoutSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-layout.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="layout"
  title="Motion: move to a new place"
  description="An element with a layout motion moves to its new place and size when the layout around it changes; its content keeps its shape."
>
  <MotionStage scene="resize" label="Live example: Move to a new place" height="md">
    <Fragment slot="controls"><ResizeControls size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Resize size="page" />
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    A layout motion has no keyframes. Its element moves from where it was to its new place and size when the layout
    around it changes, and nothing is left inline at the end. The preset <code>reflow</code> is a layout motion.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

defineMotion('card-move', { verb: 'layout' }); // the timing is optional`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The layout engine is loaded the first time a layout motion is bound. A change made before it is loaded does not
    move: <code>await loadLayoutEngine()</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion</code>, loads it in advance.
  </p>

  <h2>The scope</h2>
  <p>
    A change inside the scope moves the elements of the scope: a class or a <code>data-*</code> attribute changes on an
    element of it, a child is added, removed or reordered, or <code>hidden</code> changes. The scope is the closest
    ancestor with <code>data-motion-scope</code>, or else the element's parent. An element that appears or disappears
    does not animate itself: it has no earlier box to move from.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<div data-motion-scope>
  <div data-motion="reflow" data-wide>Widen me</div>
  <ul>
    <li data-motion="reflow">Build</li>
  </ul>
</div>`}</code></pre>

  <h2>An inline style</h2>
  <p>
    An inline style is not observed. After one, ask for the move with <code>play()</code>: it compares the layout now and
    plays the move. An interrupted move restarts with the velocity it had.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { getMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

card.style.width = '100%';                 // an inline style is not observed
getMotion(card, 'layout')?.play();         // compares the layout and plays the move`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    React <code>&lt;Motion name="reflow"&gt;</code>, Angular <code>udxMotion="reflow"</code>, Svelte
    <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('reflow')&#125;</code>. The examples change an attribute, a class and the order of the
    rows: each is observed, so none of them calls <code>play()</code>.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-layout">
    <MotionLayoutReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionLayoutAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionLayoutSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions verb="layout" />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>Without a timing, a layout moves on the default spatial spring.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, the new layout applies at once.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Elements inside a resizing element keep their natural size during the move, up to three levels deep and 24 elements.</li>
    <li>Text placed directly in the followed element, with no element around it, is stretched during the move: wrap it in an element.</li>
    <li><code>transform-origin</code> must stay at the centre, where the move scales the element.</li>
    <li>A move caused by something outside the scope is not animated.</li>
    <li>A layout motion is refused on an SVG element, since it needs a box.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
